<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65335" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγᾰ-κήτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>,
		(cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κητώεις</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>yawning, with mighty hollows</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγακήτεα πόντον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					3.158
				</span></i>
			; <i>with mighty maw</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δελφίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.22
				</span></i>
			; <i>capacious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.222
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				11.5
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				600
			</span></i>. (Also expld. as derived from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῆτος,
				μ. πόντος</span>
			<i>teeming with monsters</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. νηῦς</span>
			<i>with a monster as figurehead.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
